    key: "S6-030",
    domainCode: 6,
    stem: `A complex batch ETL join stage spills over 40 GB of shuffle data to local disk on every nightly run. The query cannot be redesigned this quarter, so the team wants a compute-level change that reduces the spill without touching the code. Which change follows the documented guidance?`,
    options: [
      "Treat the spill as harmless log noise, because writing shuffle data to disk never slows a stage down",
      "Reduce the memory per executor, which forces Spark to launch more tasks and split the shuffle data among them",
      "Disable Adaptive Query Execution, which removes partition coalescing and with it all spill from the stage",
      "Use instances with more memory, or fewer and larger workers, so more of the shuffle fits before spilling",
    ],
    correctIndex: 3,
    explanationEn: `Spill happens when execution memory runs out during shuffles, joins, sorts, and aggregations, and Spark serializes the data to local disk — which is expensive. Besides shrinking the data itself, the documented compute-level remedies are to increase executor memory: pick instance types with more memory, and for complex batch ETL with joins across multiple tables use fewer, larger workers so each task holds more of the shuffle in memory. What matters is the ratio of memory to cores, not just the total. Spill is not harmless logging. Cutting memory per executor increases spill rather than forcing useful parallelism, and disabling AQE removes runtime optimizations such as automatic shuffle partition sizing — it does not eliminate spill.`,
    explanationPt: `Spill acontece quando a memória de execução acaba durante shuffles, joins, sorts e agregações, e o Spark serializa os dados no disco local — o que é caro. Além de reduzir os dados em si, as correções documentadas no nível do compute são aumentar a memória por executor: escolher tipos de instância com mais memória e, para ETL batch complexo com joins entre várias tabelas, usar fewer, larger workers, de modo que cada task mantenha mais do shuffle em memória. O que importa é a razão entre memória e cores, não só o total. Spill não é log inofensivo. Cortar a memória por executor aumenta o spill em vez de forçar um paralelismo útil, e desligar o AQE remove otimizações de runtime como o dimensionamento automático das partições de shuffle — não elimina o spill.`,
