    explanationEn: `When more queries arrive than the running clusters can handle, the warehouse queues them — the queue holds up to 1,000 queries — and the autoscaler provisions additional clusters of the same size to process the backlog, driven by the estimated load and by queue wait times, until it reaches the configured maximum of 6 clusters; when load drops, it scales back down toward the minimum needed. Scaling out works by adding whole clusters, not by swapping in larger drivers. Queued queries wait rather than fail with a timeout. And the maximum is a real setting — the Peak Queued Queries metric on the monitoring tab tells the team whether to raise the maximum or the cluster size.`,
