    domainCode: 6,
    stem: `A long-running job on a cluster with spot workers loses one mid-run: the node is reclaimed by the cloud provider, and a shuffle stage that had tasks on that node is suddenly incomplete. A new engineer assumes the whole job run is lost.

What actually happens?`,
    options: [
      "Spark re-executes the lost tasks and dependent stages, so the run continues without starting over",
      "The entire job run fails immediately, and Lakeflow Jobs restarts the whole thing from the first task",
      "The lost tasks are skipped, so the run completes with silently missing partitions",
      "Spot reclamation pauses the job until the same node type becomes available again",
    ],
    correctIndex: 0,
    explanationEn: `Spark tracks lineage: when a node disappears, the tasks that ran on it are simply re-executed elsewhere — along with any dependent stage outputs that were lost with the node — and the job continues, paying recomputation cost but not restarting from zero. Job-level failure only occurs if the cluster itself cannot continue or retries are exhausted; tasks are never silently skipped, and nothing waits for the reclaimed node to return, because Spark reschedules the work on the workers that remain.`,
    explanationPt: `O Spark rastreia a linhagem: quando um nó desaparece, as tasks que rodaram nele são simplesmente reexecutadas em outro lugar — junto com as saídas dos estágios dependentes que se perderam com o nó — e o job continua, pagando o custo de recomputação, mas sem recomeçar do zero. A falha no nível do job só ocorre se o próprio cluster não puder continuar ou as retentativas se esgotarem; tasks nunca são silenciosamente puladas, e nada espera o nó reclamado voltar, porque o Spark reagenda o trabalho nos workers que restam.`,
